Subject: [PATCH] drm/amdgpu: BC-250 — flush all mapped VMIDs, direct MMIO path

The PASID-to-VMID query in gmc_v10_0_flush_gpu_tlb_pasid() races KFD teardown
and the INVALIDATE_TLBS packet wedges KIQ on this board. Instead, invalidate
every currently mapped process VMID through the direct register path on every
TLB invalidation, and keep the BC-250 off the KIQ branch in
gmc_v10_0_flush_gpu_tlb() entirely.

This is the exact deployed form on blade 15 (snapshot snap-a0af1eeb and
snap-8fe794e8): logs "BC-250: %d VMID(s) flushed" with dev_info_ratelimited.

Context generated against the post-patch-14 tree (the KIQ branch carries the
patch-14 v2 marker); applies with patch -p1 --fuzz=0 after patch 14.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/gmc_v10_0.c
@@ -303,7 +303,8 @@
 			goto use_mmio;
 	}
 	/* ===== BC-250 v2 PATCH END ===== */
-	if (adev->gfx.kiq[0].ring.sched.ready && !adev->enable_mes &&
+	if (adev->pdev->device != 0x13fe &&
+	    adev->gfx.kiq[0].ring.sched.ready && !adev->enable_mes &&
 	    (amdgpu_sriov_runtime(adev) || !amdgpu_sriov_vf(adev))) {
 		amdgpu_gmc_fw_reg_write_reg_wait(adev, req, ack, inv_req,
 						 1 << vmid, GET_INST(GC, 0));
@@ -420,6 +421,27 @@
 	uint16_t queried;
 	int vmid, i;
 
+	/*
+	 * BC-250/gfx1013: the PASID-to-VMID query races KFD teardown and the
+	 * INVALIDATE_TLBS packet wedges KIQ on this board. Instead, invalidate
+	 * every currently mapped process VMID through the direct register path.
+	 */
+	if (adev->pdev->device == 0x13fe) {
+		int atingidos = 0;
+
+		for (vmid = 1; vmid < AMDGPU_NUM_VMID; vmid++) {
+			if (!gmc_v10_0_get_atc_vmid_pasid_mapping_info(
+			    adev, vmid, &queried))
+				continue;
+			gmc_v10_0_flush_gpu_tlb(adev, vmid,
+						AMDGPU_GFXHUB(0), flush_type);
+			atingidos++;
+		}
+		dev_info_ratelimited(adev->dev,
+				     "BC-250: %d VMID(s) flushed\n", atingidos);
+		return;
+	}
+
 	for (vmid = 1; vmid < AMDGPU_NUM_VMID; vmid++) {
 		bool valid;
 
